<title>USA: Old Republic International sells notes.</title>
<headline>Old Republic International sells notes.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-06-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following debt issue from Old Republic International Corp was priced on Wednesday, according to lead manager Lehman Brothers.</p>
<p>Proceeds will be used to paydown commercial paper.</p>
<p>Old Republic is a diversified insurance holding company with interests in commercial lines property and casualty insurance, life insurance, title insurance, and mortgage insurance.</p>
<p>BORROWER OLD REPUBLIC INTERNATIONAL CORP</p>
<p>AMT $115 MLN	 COUPON 7.00 PCT   MATURITY 6/15/2007</p>
<p>TYPE NOTES	   ISS PRICE 99.946  FIRST PAY DATE 12/15/1997</p>
<p>LAST MOODY'S AA3   YIELD 7.008 PCT   PAY FREQ  SEMI-ANNUAL</p>
<p>S&amp;P AA-MINUS	 SPREAD 60 BP	CALLABLE  NO</p>
<p>U.S. Corporate Bond Unit, 212-859-1678</p>
